#### RL training.

We implement our RL framework using verl (Sheng et al., [2024](https://ar5iv.labs.arxiv.org/html/2603.18620v1#bib.bib43 "HybridFlow: a flexible and efficient rlhf framework")). We find that randomly sampling nodes from the evolution trees produces weak training signal early in training. Instead, we build a simple curriculum by preferentially sampling nodes with the highest improvement potential, defined as the difference between a node’s performance and the maximum performance in its own tree. We use a learning rate of 1×10−51\times 10^{-5}, sample 32 nodes per batch, and generate 4 rollouts per node. We perform on-policy training and do not apply KL regularization. We train for 4 epochs and select the best checkpoint based on a separate development set.

